#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""mkrows15.py > rows : the round 15 ledger rows (eight cells each, no bare pipe inside a cell)."""
T = 'Docs/Decompiler/tools/a3_round15'
rows = []
def row(id_, sev, finding, fixture, status='open'):
    cells = [id_, '3', sev, finding, fixture, status, 'area 3 round 15 review', '']
    for c in cells:
        assert '|' not in c.replace('\\|', ''), (id_, c)
        assert '\n' not in c
    rows.append('| ' + ' | '.join(cells) + ' |')

row('A3-130', 'P1',
 "A STORE through a pointer reached by two or more frame slots is lost while the frame has not escaped (A3-124's class, one pointer deeper; 0068 does not reach it). `S` at frame+12, slot1 (frame+32) holds &S, slot2 (frame+36) holds &slot1; the store is `mov.l @(36,r15),r1 ; mov.l @r1,r1 ; add #10,r1 ; mov.w r2,@r1` (the pointer is a LOAD through a stack read). S+8 is zeroed, the halfword -45 is stored at S+10, S+8 is read as a word: the code returns 0xFFD3; the text is lent `int4 f(void)` and `return 0;` (the word store of -1 at S+8, R15-7d: `return 0;` for 0xFFFFFFD3; three slots, R15-7c: the same). Mechanism, traced with a temporary build: heritage pass 1 guards the STORE (it is marked, being a LOAD of a stack word) on S, both slots and PR; `Heritage::reprocessFreeStores` runs in the same pass, with the stack linked the first reload is a modeled frame address, `FrameEscape::compute` has `case CPUI_LOAD: continue` (what a LOAD reads is memory), the STORE's pointer is no member, the STORE is unmarked and its four INDIRECT guards are destroyed (`opDestroy` from `reprocessFreeStores`); the direct read of S+8 is linked to the older write, the LOAD through &slot1 folds a pass later into a stack read, the STORE after it into a COPY nothing reads, and dead code removes it. 0068's delay raises only for a read found late: the late item here is a write, so one 'Restarted to delay deadcode elimination' warning is printed and the store is still lost. A call handed a frame address (R15-8a, 8c), the frame address published in a global (8b), a read through the chain (8d) or one slot (R15-7b) are right, because the frame escapes or the guard is not needed. Wrong on f3c13b0 as on ec93ad3. The frame ledger sees it (`LEDGER BAD`: the frame write of 2 bytes went unread, read at the word read); the printed-C differential sees it (`mismatch`, run 0000FFD3 text 00000000). frame124 draws one slot only; `frame15.py` with two or three levels and no fill: 6 to 10 of 60 fixtures of seed 5 per configuration have `LEDGER BAD`.",
 "`%s/r15h.src` R15-7a, 7c, 7d (controls 7b, `r15i.src` 8a to 8d); R15-7a 06009000: `4F22 7FD0 61F3 710C 1F18 61F3 7120 1F19 E300 1F35 E2D3 51F9 6112 710A 2121 50F5 7F30 4F26 000B 0009` (sts.l pr ; add #-48,r15 ; S=sp+12 ; slot1=&S ; slot2=&slot1 ; S+8=0 ; r2=-45 ; two reloads ; halfword at S+10 ; read S+8). Replay: `SE_GENERATED_PRINTEDC=only SE_GENERATED_PRINTEDC_WORDS=\"4F22 7FD0 61F3 710C 1F18 61F3 7120 1F19 E300 1F35 E2D3 51F9 6112 710A 2121 50F5 7F30 4F26 000B 0009\"`. Wrong: lent, `return 0;`. Right: `return 0xffd3;` (what the one-slot control R15-7b prints). Oracle: the run line and the frame ledger." % T)

row('A3-131', 'P1',
 "Regression of patch 0068 (A3-127's front piece, exposed, f3c13b0 is right): a word that is built from stores through a pointer reloaded from a frame slot over bytes the function never wrote, then returned, is returned as its low piece. `S+4` (uninitialised) gets the halfword r5 at +2 and the halfword r6 at +0 through the reloaded pointer, the word is read directly and returned: the code returns 0x66664444 (r6 low, r5 low); lent `int4 f(int, int, int)` and `return param_2;` (R15-12a; bytes R15-12b, R15-13d `return param_2;` for the four byte stores r5 at +3, r6 at +2, r7 at +1, r4 at +0, code 0x22886644; halfwords of one register R15-12d). The base prints `xStack_24 = CONCAT22(param_3,param_2); return xStack_24;`. With the front piece set back to upstream's `bytesAfter` the head is right again (local build), so the cause is 0068's front length in `opCollapseIndirectsForCopy`: the collapse now builds `SUB42(in_stack,2)` for the bytes before the first COPY, a free stack input (the word was never written), and the data-flow that reaches the return carries it (pass 3: `CONCAT22(r6.lo,SUB42(CONCAT22(SUB42(in,2),r5.lo),0))`); at pass 4 the return is `r0+2 = r5+2 ; return r0+2`, the low two bytes only (printed with `fd->printRaw` in a temporary build). By reading, not instrumented: the return recovery (`AncestorRealistic`) takes the high half, whose chain ends in a free stack input, for unreal data flow and shrinks the return to its low piece. The same word stored to a global, passed to a lent callee or added to a parameter is right (R15-14a to 14c); a zeroed word first (R15-12c), direct stores (R15-13a) or a pointer in a register (R15-13c) are right. The frame ledger says ok (no access is lost, no piece is malformed: the pieces add up); the printed-C differential finds it (`mismatch`, `size=2 upper-bits` in the generator's own words: `F15.31.297`, seed 31 of `frame15.py`: 1 of 700 call-free L1 fixtures). A real shape: a struct of two shorts or four chars built through a local pointer and returned as a word.",
 "`%s/r15m.src` R15-12a to 12e, `r15n.src` R15-13d (controls 12c, 13a, 13c, `r15o.src` 14a to 14c); R15-12a 06009000 with args 11112222 33334444 55556666 77778888: `4F22 7FD0 61F3 710C 1F18 51F8 7106 2151 51F8 7104 2161 E000 61F3 710C 7104 6312 203A 7F30 4F26 000B 0009 0009` (lent from r4 to r7). Wrong: lent, `return param_2;` (r0=33334444 as text; the code returns 66664444). Right: `xStack_24 = CONCAT22(param_3,param_2); return xStack_24;` (the base's and the zeroed control's). Oracle: the run line; printed-C replay of R15-10a (`r15k.src`, the shrunk seed-31 case): `SE_GENERATED_PRINTEDC=only SE_GENERATED_PRINTEDC_WORDS=\"4F22 7FD0 61F3 710C 1F18 51F8 7106 2121 51F8 7104 2121 51F8 7108 2152 E000 61F3 710C 7104 6312 203A 7F30 4F26 000B 0009\"`." % T)

row('A3-132', 'P1',
 "The entry value of a callee-saved register stored into a frame word (any store: `mov.l r8,@(8,r15)`, a push, via r10; r8 to r14, GBR and VBR, not MACL or a scratch input) and then overwritten through a pointer reloaded from a frame slot is read back as the register: `return unaff_r8;` where the code returns r5. `add #-16,r15 ; mov.l r8,@(8,r15) ; mov r15,r1 ; add #8,r1 ; mov.l r1,@r15 ; mov.l @r15,r2 ; mov.l r5,@r2 ; mov.l @(8,r15),r0` (no call): the signature is withheld ('it reads r8 on entry') and the text is `return unaff_r8;`; byte and halfword overwrites through the reload too (R15-6c, 6d), a halfword or byte store of r8 is data and is right (R15-5i, 5j), the pointer in a register (R15-6b) or published in a global first (R15-6a) is right. Trace: the guards of the STORE are made on all three ranges at pass 1 and `opCollapseIndirectsForAlias` destroys the one on the save slot at once (`noalias=1`, `guard=0`): `ActionRestrictLocal` marks the storage of a COPY of an unaffected register as not mapped (`markNotMapped`, the save slot), 0063's exception for a slot an indexed STORE may write (`isGuarded` of a valid STORE guard) does not hold a pointer reloaded from a frame slot, so the slot has no local alias, the guard goes, the store folds later into a COPY nothing reads. Wrong on f3c13b0 and ec93ad3 alike (the A3-124 class through the save-slot mechanism of A3-102; patch 0068's save exemption (`isSavePush`) is not involved: pushes and plain stores behave the same). The frame ledger finds it (`LEDGER BAD`, 6 of 11 variants). In compiled code the save slot is never overwritten; a local that starts as a callee-saved register's entry value (a function that uses r8 before setting it) is the same word. 5 of 21 one-slot and 4 of 23 two-slot `fill=save` fixtures of `frame15.py` seed 1 have `LEDGER BAD`.",
 "`%s/r15f.src` R15-5a to 5k, `r15e.src` R15-4a, `r15g.src` R15-6a to 6d; R15-5a 06009000 args 0 0 0 0 r8=11 and 1 2 3 4 r8=66: `4F22 7FF0 1F82 61F3 7108 2F12 62F2 2252 50F2 7F10 4F26 000B 0009 0009`. Wrong: withheld, `return unaff_r8;`. Right: `return param_2;` (R15-5d, the same with r3 for r8, lent). Oracle: the run line (r0 = r5) and the frame ledger." % T)

row('A3-133', 'P2',
 "Instrument: the frame ledger's own caps fail open. `Funcdata::noteFrameFoldForwarded` walks back from a forwarded value through at most 64 ops, then sets `frameFoldsAllRead` (and 4,096 guard records do the same) and the function's every frame write is taken as read: a function whose loss is hidden by a 64-op expression is reported clean. R15-15a (A3-130's shape) is `LEDGER BAD`; the same function with 10 xor/add operations on the result is `LEDGER BAD`; with 40 (R15-15c) or 80 (R15-15d) it is `LEDGER ok` while the text is the same wrong text (`return ((param_2 * 2 + ...` without the 0xffd3 term; printed-C `mismatch`, run 000113D3 text 00001400). Counted with a temporary print where the walk hits the cap (`dbg_engine.diff`, `SE_DBG_CAP=1`): 90 of the 839 functions of hwram007 and 228 of the 1,554 of hwram008 (11% and 15%) are not checked for lost frame writes at all; the round's '0 frame writes lost' holds for the rest. A3-129's text calls this 'may miss a loss, never report one that is none' and counts on the generator; a cap that fails open is what round 14's A3-122 was.",
 "`%s/r15p.src` R15-15a to 15d (`NOLEDGER` unset: the driver prints `LEDGER BAD`/`ok`); `dbg_engine.diff` for the count (not applied; `SE_DBG_CAP=1 SE_GAME_HWRAM=<img> SE_GAME_LEND=1 SaturnExplorerSh2DecompilerTests <dir> 2> err ; grep FRAMECAP err ; sort -u`). Wrong: ledger ok on R15-15c and 15d. Right: BAD, as on 15a and 15b (the cap should keep the function unchecked and say so, or fail the run; a taken-as-read answer should count as 'unchecked' in the corpus line)." % T)

row('A3-134', 'P3',
 "Instrument: the generator draws none of A3-130 to A3-132 and the frame ledger cannot see A3-131. `GenFrame124Fn` has one pointer slot, always fills S whole first, and never stores a callee-saved register's entry value into S; `frame15.py` (two or three slots, no fill, `fill=save`) finds all three at once: 31 of 200 fixtures of seed 1 have `LEDGER BAD`. A3-131 is a value error with no lost access, so only the printed-C differential can see it, and it sees call-free functions only. One more finding of the same driver: a byte store into a 3-byte array local prints `axStack_24 = (xunknown1  [3])CONCAT21(0,param_1);` and `_axStack_24 = CONCAT31(axStack_24,0x8f);` (an array assigned a cast to an array type, invalid C; printed-C `not-compilable`, F15.31.408, 1 of 700): misleading, no wrong value found.",
 "`%s/frame15.py` (`python3 frame15.py <seed> <count>`, knobs `F15_LEVELS`, `F15_NST`, `F15_CALL`, `F15_FILL`), `f15run.sh`, `f15sum.py`, `f15pc.py`, `shrink15.py`; F15.31.408 words `4F22 7FD0 61F3 7110 1F18 E238 51F8 710B 2120 E246 51F8 7106 2120 E259 51F8 710E 2120 E205 51F8 7104 2120 E250 51F8 710F 2120 E24B 51F8 7108 2120 E25B 51F8 7101 2120 E21E 51F8 7109 2120 E223 51F8 710D 2120` (the head of the function; run `f15pc.py` on seed 31, `F15_CALL=none F15_LEVELS=1 F15_FILL=words,bytes,halves`). Right: a generator stream with the three shapes, folded into `GenFrame124Fn`." % T)

row('A3-135', 'P3',
 "A lent prototype that drops r8 when the function hands the address of r8's push slot to a callee that reads it: `mov.l r8,@-r15 ; sts.l pr,@-r15 ; mov r15,r4 ; add #4,r4 ; jsr g ; ... ` with `g: mov.l @r4,r0 ; rts ; nop` is lent as `xunknown4 f(void)` and returns g's value, the caller's r8 (R15-1a); the frame address published in a global and read by g (R15-1b) is the same. A callee-saved register's push is no read, by 0068's `isSavePush` and, before it, by the lending trials; here the slot is read as data by a callee and the lent signature misses an input. Wrong on f3c13b0 as well (the trials treat a push as a save), so not a regression; the A3-124 fix's record lists it as a limit ('none of the fixtures, generator seeds or corpus functions read here does'). Not found in either save state. P3 for that and because it needs a function that gives away its own save area.",
 "`%s/r15a.src` R15-1a, 1b (also 1c: the push as the fifth stack argument of an unlent callee, withheld and right); R15-1a 06009000, 06009100 lent, args 0 0 0 0 r8=12345678: `2F86 4F22 64F3 7404 D103 410B 0009 4F26 7F04 000B 0009 0009 0600 9100`. Wrong: lent, `xVar1 = func_0x06009100(axStack_208 + 0x81)` with no parameter. Right: withheld ('it reads r8 on entry'), or a parameter for r8. Status: P3, to accept with a reason or fix with A3-132." % T, status='open')

print('\n'.join(rows))
